    "done_when": "The review of the-stop-bound-test-states-its-discriminator (96) found that the declared control for tests/test_a_stopped_run_ends_its_supervisor.py, a 600 s stop grace, reddens the ignored-stop case at the 90 s wait ceiling (_wait_until raises) and never reaches the new 40 s elapsed bound. Nothing executed shows that bound failing. The node adds a second control mutation through the same environment hook as MUTATION_STOP_GRACE_SECONDS: a stop grace chosen so the supervisor exits after the elapsed bound but before CEILING_SECONDS, with the value derived from those two constants rather than written as a literal. Under that mutation the ignored-stop case passes the wait and fails on the elapsed bound. The node runs it, and its log shows the failing assertion is the elapsed bound, not the ceiling. The unmutated file passes. Both control logs, the existing ceiling control and the new bound control, are executed and logged in the run directory.",
